INSERT INTO feature VALUES('interop-boundary','runtime','The boundary with Rust, called both ways','foreign-calls','partial','uncommon','mainstream languages','A Rust caller holding a composed program calls one of its definitions by name on values it builds and reads the answer back into its own arena, the arguments applied in order, an answered function left unforced and a refused definition unrunnable before a run. A definition marked `export` whose parameters and result are fixed-width integers and whose row is empty takes a key in its program''s export table, its position there; the mark on any other definition is refused `OutOfFragment.Export`, or `OutOfFragment.ExportRow` where the row is open or names an interface. An `extern "rust"` block of fixed-width members declares an interface its source''s definitions perform and the Rust caller''s host answers; a member beyond the form is refused by name. A source whose import opens the block''s source reads the interface as well: its rows name it and its calls perform it, and the Rust caller''s host answers them. A block carrying `boundary` is admitted where it is declared: each member''s declared types, printed by Rust''s default layout, realise the row the attribute names for it, or the block is refused `BoundaryUnrealised` by the clause a member breaks. The check reads `std.boundary` wherever the imports of the block''s source reach it, whatever they list, and it runs at the block''s own source alone, however many sources import it. A value crosses by its layout as words: the Rust caller lends its memory and passes a word, and gandr reads the memory behind it only through a block''s reads, which the host answers at the addresses it lent. A list Rust holds tagged or packed decodes into its layout''s data type, and the `length` transported along that layout''s path answers what Rust counts; `Option<&u32>`''s null word reads as `None`. A handler written in gandr answers a block''s interface inside its scope, where its clauses shadow the host: each clause receives its member''s arguments as one payload at their fixed widths, and a clause for a member the block lacks, or one that binds no payload for a member that takes arguments, is refused at the clause.','surface-corpus surface-dispatcher surface-lowering surface-lowering-base surface-lowering-expression','crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/boundary.rs crates/surface-lowering/src/lower/capability/tests.rs crates/surface-lowering/src/lower/boundary/tests.rs crates/surface-lowering/src/lower/export/tests.rs corpus/model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr corpus/model/interop/boundary/imported.gandr corpus/model/interop/boundary/by-layout.gandr corpus/model/programs/export-add.gandr corpus/pathological/interop/boundary/extern-form.gandr corpus/pathological/interop/boundary/source-handler.gandr','corpus/ledger/features/interop-boundary.gandr','#327 #7841');
